      "execution": {
        "startingPosition": "Stand with your feet hip-distance apart on the floor in front of a free barbell. Bend your knees slightly, hinge forward with a straight back, grip the bar with both hands shoulder-width apart, and draw your shoulders back and down.",
        "movement": "Lift the bar from the floor over two seconds by extending your hips. Finish tall by fully extending your hips and knees without turning the lift into a squat.",
        "endpoint": "Stand upright with your hips and knees fully extended and the bar held in front of your body.",
        "returnPhase": "Hinge forward and lower the bar for two seconds until the plates touch the floor beside your feet, keeping the slight knee bend and straight-back position. The source did not prescribe a floor pause, reset, or complete unloading.",
        "controlledJoints": "Keep the lift hip-dominant. Begin with the prescribed slight knee bend, but do not treat it as a measured fixed angle.",
        "supportAndPosture": "Keep both feet planted, brace your trunk, maintain the instructed straight-back posture, and use no external torso support.",
        "disqualifyingCompensations": [
          "Keeping the knees extended throughout turns the movement into a stiff-leg deadlift.",
          "Bending the knees deeply turns the hinge into a squat-like conventional floor pull.",
          "Stopping the plates above the floor turns the reviewed floor-touch fixture into a partial or continuous Romanian deadlift."
        ]
      }
